<title>HONG KONG: SOCCER-VIOLENCE HALTS ASIAN CUP GAME.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-VIOLENCE HALTS ASIAN CUP GAME.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crowd trouble interrupted the</p>
<p>Asian Cup Winners' Cup second round between local side South</p>
<p>China and Mastrans Bandung Raya of Indonesia for 45 minutes on</p>
<p>Sunday.</p>
<p>Bottles were hurled at the Mastrans bench after their</p>
<p>defender Kissito Atangana was sent off in the second half. The</p>
<p>visiting team left the pitch.</p>
<p>South China won 4-0, 5-1 on aggregate.</p>
</text>
